  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Local state",
      "items": [
        "state lives in the OS dirs — config, data, cache, state, runtime — never in a hard-coded ~/.config, and the path APIs pick the right one per platform",
        "writes are atomic: a temp file, fsync, rename, plus a lock so two instances of the CLI cannot corrupt each other",
        "the config is schema-validated and versioned; a migration runs forward and a downgrade is refused with a clear message",
        "purge removes the local state of a project; secrets are wiped on sign-out"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Secrets and the wire",
      "items": [
        "the token lives in the OS keystore behind SecretStorePort; a secret in the config file, a log line or telemetry is a finding",
        "an env var is a CI path, not the default; the flag and the env fallback exist for the pipeline, not for the developer",
        "every request carries the correlation id, which lands in the local log and in the error output so support can find it"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Where the data goes",
      "items": [
        "stdout carries the result and nothing else — text, one JSON envelope or NDJSON events; progress, prompts and warnings go to stderr",
        "the local log under the state dir is rotated and redacted; telemetry is opt-in and never contains tokens or file content",
        "the API is the only system of record: the CLI caches and configures, it does not keep a second copy of the business data"
      ]
    }
  ]
